WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.450
- Hey guys it's Justine
and today I'm unboxing

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.590
something really exciting.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.820
I just ordered this and
it arrived very quickly

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.890
which I'm very excited about

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.470
because I really wanted
what was inside this box

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.390
and it's crazy because
this isn't a new product,

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:12.560
but I thought it'd be really fun

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.190
to just unbox it, show it to you,

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.830
see the types of things that I'm getting

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.050
during the lockdown.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.690
Who would've thought
that there was a shortage

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.730
of this product?

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.652
I don't know.

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:27.235
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.291 --> 00:00:32.150
- Huh, yes here it is.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:37.150
You're greeted with a nice
little protective layer

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.203
to protect your item.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.633
Here it is.

00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:48.690
(laughing) So here it is, we
can take a look (laughing).

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.780
This is the front of the box

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.640
and you'll see here
that this lets you know

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.350
that you can make this in
2 1/2 minute cook time.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.590
Here we have all of our specs.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.530
There's a 100 milligrams of sodium,

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.950
25 grams of carbs, and
there's zero sugars.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:11.270
That's a really great selling point.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.960
Here is a very big
highlight on the spec sheet.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.730
It says that studies have
shown that many Americans

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.860
do not consume enough calcium.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.450
And here we have some of the instructions.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:21.283
Nothing new.

00:01:21.283 --> 00:01:23.660
Most products usually come
with instruction booklets,

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.040
but this one is just very
nicely marked here on the back

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.640
so you don't have to
dig around on the inside

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.590
to try to find any loose paper work.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.220
I just appreciate how thorough they are

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.990
with everything that they
have on the back of here

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:38.890
because they let you know
the best tips for results.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.270
So when you're preparing this with milk,

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.540
just make sure that you watch carefully,

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.970
stir to prevent the
milk from boiling over.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.070
They also have a couple
different models of this.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.110
This is the original.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:51.360
I am a huge fan of just simple, basic,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.480
but if you are interested in other models,

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.710
maybe some upgrades, they
have an instant brown sugar,

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.260
they also have an instant variety pack,

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.800
they have whole grain, and cinnamon.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.280
One of the things you
should always check for

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.390
are expiration dates,
so up here they nicely

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:11.840
have that labeled, right
here, March 3rd, of 2022.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.960
Impressive shelf life.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.450
I mean you won't have to
worry about your product

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.600
going out of date for quite awhile.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.800
So this is the on button.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.360
You just have to press here,

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.390
which I think is kind of misleading

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.730
because I'm pressing
and it's not very easy.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.580
It's perforated, but not very well.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.020
It's possible that they did
that for security reasons.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.210
I mean it makes sense.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.300
That was really difficult.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.410
I mean I had to actually cut this open

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.170
to get it to turn on.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.253
Do the smell test.

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:43.913
Kind of smells like a new Mac.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.550
Well now that we pretty
much have this all set up,

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:52.440
all opened, all unboxed, I
think that the next logical step

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:56.083
is to go test it out and see how it works.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.300
Okay, the time has come to
really give this a test.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.590
We're gonna follow the instructions.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:04.640
Oops.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.710
Oh gosh, I've already not
followed these directions.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:08.174
Oh shoot, that was a little too much.

00:03:08.174 --> 00:03:10.780
(upbeat music)

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:11.787
(water pouring)

00:03:11.787 --> 00:03:13.850
You don't really have to be
that precise about measurements.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.870
I think it's gonna come out just fine.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:20.400
So I'm gonna be putting this in here

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.610
to really make sure we can
maximize all of the testing

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.180
that we can possibly do.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.300
High for one minute

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.840
and then we stir again.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.010
And then we continue to cook

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:31.990
for an additional one to two minutes.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.683
I can't wait for breakfast tomorrow.

00:03:38.346 --> 00:03:41.020
(sanitizer spraying)

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.360
Oh, so one of the things that
you need to watch out for,

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.110
is you gotta make sure
it doesn't boil over.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.730
So this is kind of just
a midway little stir

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:50.970
with a wire whisk.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.570
It didn't say how how much to stir,

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:56.623
so I'm using my own good judgment.

00:03:57.788 --> 00:04:00.788
(microwave beeping)

00:04:02.148 --> 00:04:03.370
My mom always told me not to stand

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:06.560
too close to the microwave
because it would affect me,

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.810
my brain, but I gotta keep an eye on it

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.288
because it's gonna overflow.

00:04:10.288 --> 00:04:11.121
Ah!

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.540
This looks like a perfect
consistency to me,

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.523
do you think?

00:04:16.523 --> 00:04:19.190
(whisk tapping)

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:22.990
You can always add some
upgrades if you choose.

